# %ECSV 1.0
# ---
# datatype:
# - {name: detector, datatype: string}
# - {name: filter, datatype: string}
# - {name: anchor, datatype: string}
# - {name: frame, datatype: string}
# - {name: dx_mas, datatype: float64}
# - {name: dy_mas, datatype: float64}
# - {name: n, datatype: int64}
# - {name: sem_mas, datatype: float64}
# meta: !!omap
# - comments: ['Per-(detector, filter) placement CORRECTIONS onto the JWST 2-micron consensus frame.', dx_mas/dy_mas are the correction
#       to ADD -- the NEGATIVE of the measured, '  (filter - anchor) residual.  Applying the residual doubles the error.', 'frame=instrument:
#       sky vector rotated by +ROLL_REF; rotate by -ROLL_REF to apply', '  (filter_frame_correction.instrument_to_sky).', 'Module-mean
#       removed per module, after negation.', 'F182M: mean of three observations -- brick jw02221-o001 (ROLL_REF 89.13),', '  sgrc jw04147-o012
#       (91.50), wd2 jw03523-o005 (141.01).  A table built from', '  brick+sgrc alone predicts wd2 -- held out, 52 deg away in roll --
#       with 0.41 mas', '  residual and 95 percent of the variance explained; the opposite rotation gives', '  2.15 mas and explains nothing.',
#     'F187N: brick jw02221-o001 only (n=1).  Jay Anderson has no F187N STDGDC solution', '  and no second observation has been solved.  Residual
#       amplitude 0.55 mas.', 'F182M/F187N solved by scripts/analysis/solve_filter_frame_offsets.py --write; see issue #296.', 'F162M:
#       mean of wd2 jw03523-o005 (ROLL_REF 141.01) and sgrc jw04147-o012 (91.50).', '  Each field predicted from the other field alone:
#       10.24 -> 0.36 mas (wd2) and', '  10.18 -> 0.36 mas (sgrc), 2-D rms.', 'F164N: mean of wd2 jw03523-o005 (141.01) and wd1 jw01905-o001
#       (284.71).  Each', '  field predicted from the other: 10.28 -> 0.97 mas (wd2), 9.86 -> 0.97 mas (wd1).', 'F162M/F164N origin: the
#       distortion references pin every filter to the same', '  V2Ref/V3Ref per detector, while their plate scale is 202-241 ppm larger
#       than', '  F212N''s, so each detector centre sits s*R too close to the module centre.', 'F162M/F164N: n = fields, sem_mas = |row_1
#       - row_2| / (2 sqrt 2).  Rows are', '  sky_residual_to_instrument_correction applied to explicit (frame - anchor) pair', '  residuals
#       of m6 per-frame catalogs against the F212N m6 merged vetted catalog;', '  see issue #1133.']
